# ---- picker
commands.arrakis.tools.desc = The tool set: give, state, open
commands.arrakis.tools.give.desc = Give every Arrakis tool and the Blood Bag (the hotbar if there is room, else the inventory)
commands.arrakis.tools.state.desc = Show the held item, the tools found with their container and slot, the toggles and Mana
commands.arrakis.tools.open.desc = Open the tool picker page without right-clicking
customUI.arrakisPicker.title = Tools
customUI.arrakisPicker.toolsHeading = Your tools
customUI.arrakisPicker.passiveHeading = Always available
customUI.arrakisPicker.only = You carry only this one tool.
customUI.arrakisPicker.inHand = In hand
customUI.arrakisPicker.on = ON
customUI.arrakisPicker.off = OFF
customUI.arrakisPicker.handChanged = The tool in your hand changed; nothing was swapped.
customUI.arrakisPicker.toolGone = That tool is no longer where it was; nothing was swapped.

# ---- cutter
items.Arrakis_Tool_Cutter_Ray.name = Cutter Ray
items.Arrakis_Tool_Cutter_Ray.description = Placeholder gun that cuts the block in front of it with the strength of a crude pickaxe. 10 Mana per shot. Right click opens the tool picker.

# ---- compactor
items.Arrakis_Tool_Compactor.name = Compactor
items.Arrakis_Tool_Compactor.description = Hold left click on sand to compact it: one item per second, the block is not broken. 1 Mana per second. Right click opens the tool picker.

# ---- litrejon
items.Arrakis_Tool_Litrejon.name = LitreJon
items.Arrakis_Tool_Litrejon.description = A water flask. Left click pours up to 50 units into you, only what you lack. The bar shows how full it is. Right click opens the tool picker.
arrakis.litrejon.needsWater = Water of Arrakis is needed to pour from the LitreJon.
arrakis.litrejon.empty = The LitreJon is empty.
arrakis.litrejon.full = You are not thirsty.

# ---- harvester
items.Arrakis_Tool_Dew_Harvester.name = Dew Harvester
items.Arrakis_Tool_Dew_Harvester.description = Hold left click on a Primrose to collect dew: 10 water into a LitreJon you carry per swing, 10 Mana each. Right click opens the tool picker.
arrakis.harvester.noPrimrose = Aim at a Primrose.
arrakis.harvester.noFlask = You carry no LitreJon.
arrakis.harvester.flasksFull = Your LitreJon is full.

# ---- bloodbag
items.Arrakis_Blood_Bag.name = Blood Bag
items.Arrakis_Blood_Bag.description = Holds blood collected with the Blood Extractor. The bar shows how full it is. It does nothing else yet.
commands.arrakis.blood.desc = Blood helpers: add, corpse
commands.arrakis.blood.corpse.desc = Spawns a cow two blocks ahead and kills it, to try the Blood Extractor
commands.arrakis.blood.add.desc = Adds blood to the first Blood Bag with room: arrakis blood add <n>

# ---- extractor
items.Arrakis_Tool_Blood_Extractor.name = Blood Extractor
items.Arrakis_Tool_Blood_Extractor.description = Left click on a fresh mob corpse: you crouch, poke it, and 10 blood goes into a Blood Bag you carry. One use per body. Right click opens the tool picker.
arrakis.extractor.noCorpse = No fresh corpse in reach.
arrakis.extractor.used = That body has already been used.
arrakis.extractor.needCrouch = Crouch first.
arrakis.extractor.noBag = You carry no Blood Bag.
arrakis.extractor.bagsFull = Your Blood Bags are full.

# EXPERIMENT BEGIN
items.Arrakis_Exp_Flame_Cutter.name = EXPERIMENT Flame Cutter
items.Arrakis_Exp_Flame_Cutter.description = EXPERIMENT. A flamethrower turned into a rock-cutting beam: no fire, no damage to creatures; hold Primary to cut. Costs Mana.
items.Arrakis_Exp_Flame_Beam.name = EXPERIMENT Flame Beam Cutter
items.Arrakis_Exp_Flame_Beam.description = EXPERIMENT. The Flame Cutter with the Stoneskin laser instead of the ring of dots: a static weapon that cuts rock up to 5 blocks away. Costs Mana.
commands.arrakis.exp.desc = Throw-away experiments: exp cal (calibration tools)
commands.arrakis.exp.cal.desc = Calibrate where a beam sits on the player: fp, tp, cam, body, frame, pulse, apex, step, astep, view, end, collapse, target, nodes, beam, off, show, save, load, reset
commands.arrakis.exp.cal.view.desc = Change or read a parameter of the first person (fp) or third person (tp) numbers, or the start of a world-space beam (cam: camera frame; body: the grip, along the heading of the body; frame cam|body chooses): node x y z yaw pitch roll scale detached; value a number, + or -
commands.arrakis.exp.cal.number.desc = Set or step a number: a value, + or -
commands.arrakis.exp.cal.rig.desc = Switch a live rig on or off: collapse, target, nodes, beam, off
commands.arrakis.exp.cal.file.desc = Print the paste-ready block, save it, load it, or go back to the vanilla numbers
# EXPERIMENT END
